  "observations": [
    "Actual current Lilla Roberts street front is muted grey-buff stone/render with horizontal dark floor belts, broad multi-light windows and a continuous tall glazed ground floor; it is not an ornamental classical apartment facade.",
    "The main long frontage has four upper window bands. The projecting raised end blocks rise a further window storey; native step and recess geometry is preserved.",
    "A wide flat canopy marks the entrance left of the main front centre. Original unbranded line/colour cues represent it without copying signage, people, cars, flags or reflections.",
    "Eight principal main window modules and two axes on each end block are an explicit approximate reconstruction from the full and oblique views, not a surveyed bay-spacing claim.",
    "Nine exact native visual/HCOL samples fall7.5272 to5.7377m fromwesttoeast. All upper window rows and cornices remain level at a separately declared datum. Each ground glazing/door bottom follows its interpolated measured street floor; no sloped storeys or below-ground entrances are painted.",
    "A second western oblique at heading311 confirms tall dark-framed ground glazing in the western end block, and that the hotel entrance is dark metal/glass, not a timber door."
  ],
  "limitations": [
